---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} earns money through affiliate links, what that means for you, and why it does not affect our recommendations.`}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Affiliate Disclosure' }]} />
    <article class="read prose">
      <h1>Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' })}</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} earns money through affiliate links. When you click a product link on this
        site and buy something, we may receive a commission. You pay the same price either way.
      </p>

      <h2>Amazon Associates</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate
        advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by
        advertising and linking to Amazon.com.
      </p>
      <p>
        As an Amazon Associate, we earn from qualifying purchases.
      </p>
      <p>
        Amazon and the Amazon logo are trademarks of Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. Product
        prices and availability shown on this site are accurate as of the date and time indicated
        and are subject to change. Any price and availability information displayed on Amazon at
        the time of purchase is what applies to your purchase.
      </p>

      <h2>Other affiliate programs</h2>
      <p>
        We may also participate in other affiliate programs from time to time. The same rules
        apply to all of them: disclosure on the page, no influence on rankings.
      </p>

      <h2>How this affects what we recommend</h2>
      <p>
        It does not. Commission rates are not a ranking factor, and no brand can pay for a
        placement, a rating, or a mention. Where a cheaper product is the right answer for most
        people, our guides say so, even when the more expensive option would earn more.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our full process is documented in the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Where disclosures appear</h2>
      <p>
        A disclosure appears near the top of every page that contains affiliate links, before
        the first link, as required by the United States Federal Trade Commission guidelines on
        endorsements and by the Amazon Associates Operating Agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        If anything here is unclear, <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a> and we will explain it.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
